@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+## Context
+
+`createRentalService` keeps bookings in an array and derives the next id from `bookings.length + 1`. `isFree` is the single overlap test used by `book` and `availability`.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Keep cancelled bookings in the array, marked as cancelled, instead of removing them: removal would make `bookings.length + 1` reuse an id, so a cancelled id could be handed to a new booking. `isFree` skips cancelled bookings, so `book` and `availability` both free the equipment with no other change.
+- Refund = booking total when `startMs - atMs >= 24h`, otherwise 0. Exactly 24 hours before is not "less than 24 hours", so it is fully refunded. A cancellation at or after the start therefore gets no refund. The total already includes any long-stay discount, so the refund never exceeds what was paid.
+- `at` is validated as an ISO-8601 UTC string but is not required to be on the hour (assumption: a cancellation can happen at any moment, unlike rental periods). Reusing `parseInstant` would force on-the-hour, so split the format check from the on-the-hour check.
+- Validate everything (booking known, not already cancelled, `at` valid) before changing state, so a failed cancel leaves no trace.
+- Cancelling at a time after the booking's end is not rejected; it simply yields no refund (assumption).
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Cancelled bookings stay in memory; negligible at the size of a school's stock.
