@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+## Why
+
+Customers change their plans and ask the desk to cancel bookings. The cancellation policy is already recorded in the spec but the service offers no way to apply it.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `cancel(bookingId, at)` to the rental service; it cancels the booking at time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`.
+- The refund follows the recorded policy: nothing when `at` is less than 24 hours before the booking's start, the full booking total otherwise.
+- A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment, so the item can be booked and shows as available again for that period.
+- A booking can only be cancelled once; an unknown booking, a second cancellation or an invalid `at` is an error.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `rental`: replaces the "policy recorded only" cancellation requirement with a real `cancel` operation; booking, no-double-booking and availability treat cancelled bookings as not holding equipment.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: new `cancel` method and result type on `RentalService`; booking records gain a cancelled state.
+- `test/rental.test.ts`: new tests.
